                    {
                        "form_id": "70f84c57-cb8a-470e-bf8d-e224d10c3bbe",
                        "entry_id": "ee94ced9-cc24-3e90-a7d6-ce2c7b5858e7",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "cis-genre"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "8ccb4db4-e2ec-41ba-883a-89f0e8986707",
                        "entry_id": "ee94ced9-cc24-3e90-a7d6-ce2c7b5858e7",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "6genre"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2fd57234-4e3d-3bc8-828b-f5cb5ff0785c",
                        "entry_id": "ee94ced9-cc24-3e90-a7d6-ce2c7b5858e7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qualifie une personne dont l’identité de genre, est en concordance avec le genre qui lui a été assigné à la naissance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Transitude"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ba3ecc8e-8a8c-4f8b-8d36-e4979fba524d",
                                "sense_id": "2fd57234-4e3d-3bc8-828b-f5cb5ff0785c",
                                "text": "Ces nouvelles terminologies permettent aussi de rendre compte de la différence qui existe entre eux et des personnes cisgenres, en mêlant corps et orientation sexuelle : on trouvera les termes « transgouine » ou « transpédé »."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cba638ec-e884-4200-9fee-bac4f7cc1818",
                                "sense_id": "2fd57234-4e3d-3bc8-828b-f5cb5ff0785c",
                                "text": "La plupart des gens sont considérés comme « cisgenres » (« cisgendered » en anglais), leur identité sexuelle étant la même que leur sexe biologique"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8bc9a5b8-12e0-4876-99e6-c44e45358a55",
                                "sense_id": "2fd57234-4e3d-3bc8-828b-f5cb5ff0785c",
                                "text": "Chez une transgenre lesbienne, qui rêve d’une fille cisgenre, la sur-valorisation du féminin est un obstacle à l’approche, et ce d’autant plus qu’un long passé de dysphorie a souvent entraîné une inexpérience sexuelle et affective […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ccba57bf-6387-4004-be15-63a609af82e8",
                                "sense_id": "2fd57234-4e3d-3bc8-828b-f5cb5ff0785c",
                                "text": "Quand un membre du Collège veut renouveler son adhésion, on lui demande s’il est:\n– Féminin\n– Masculin\n– Agenre\n– Non conforme à un genre\n– De genre fluide\n– Non-binaire\n– Transmasculin\n– Transféminin\n– Bispirituel(le)\n– Bigenre\n– Cisgenre\n– De genre multiple\n– Autre."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0eb6163a-e8ad-4495-b58d-8b1273411355",
                        "source_entry_id": "ee94ced9-cc24-3e90-a7d6-ce2c7b5858e7",
                        "source_sense_id": "2fd57234-4e3d-3bc8-828b-f5cb5ff0785c",
                        "target_lang_word": "cisgender",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cisgender",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e33083b2-d9f7-3ec1-ae56-7358a4506e1a",
                                        "entry_id": "7e1631ab-83b7-3ba8-93cb-558be74eb904",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a gender identity which matches the sex one was assigned at birth; or, pertaining to such people."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "570f7562-1908-4955-82d8-ef383a9758db",
                                                "sense_id": "e33083b2-d9f7-3ec1-ae56-7358a4506e1a",
                                                "text": "To uphold the inequality that we choose to engage in, we regularly present the myth that trans people are deviant or a danger to cisgender people."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b63adba-55cb-48f3-bd16-ba9c727f29dc",
                                                "sense_id": "e33083b2-d9f7-3ec1-ae56-7358a4506e1a",
                                                "text": "As trans people, we have many cisgender allies—those who show their support for the concerns, needs, and rights of trans people, even though they may not personally face the same issues."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7478e76c-01b6-4b81-8db5-08ef0abb7476",
                                                "sense_id": "e33083b2-d9f7-3ec1-ae56-7358a4506e1a",
                                                "text": "R. Moskowitz charges cisgender readers to be as conscious and deliberate with our religious identities as transgender and gender non-conforming people are with theirs, arguing that holiness is only achieved through continuous and unrelenting struggle and change."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20c9ef54-4ee2-4af8-b41f-4627e185c0c6",
                                                "sense_id": "e33083b2-d9f7-3ec1-ae56-7358a4506e1a",
                                                "text": "Gender assumed many roles in this pandemic. Cisgender men were more likely to die from the virus, which seemed to be about inherent vulnerabilities of those with XY chromosomes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f649c19f-48df-47b8-a90d-5c782171f441",
                                                "sense_id": "e33083b2-d9f7-3ec1-ae56-7358a4506e1a",
                                                "text": "Transgender people report discomfort with their birth sex and a strong identification with the opposite sex. The current study was designed to shed further light on the question of whether the brains of transgender people resemble their birth sex or their gender identity. For this purpose, we analyzed a sample of 24 cisgender men, 24 cisgender women, and 24 transgender women before gender-affirming hormone therapy. We employed a recently developed multivariate classifier that yields a continuous probabilistic (rather than a binary) estimate for brains to be male or female. The brains of transgender women ranged between cisgender men and cisgender women (albeit still closer to cisgender men), and the differences to both cisgender men and to cisgender women were significant (p = 0.016 and p < 0.001, respectively). These findings add support to the notion that the underlying brain anatomy in transgender people is shifted away from their biological sex towards their gender identity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "cisgender",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b6e302ba-b629-3892-86dc-6241ae86aa52",
                                        "entry_id": "d37d4f6d-8eb5-3ae5-b14c-d044f94976d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A cisgender person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a71b1d0-99c7-457d-b21d-c8815961a81e",
                                                "sense_id": "b6e302ba-b629-3892-86dc-6241ae86aa52",
                                                "text": "Even in regard to cisgenders, research shows that it's “easier” for people to identify male than female features, meaning that the default “visible” person in our culture is male “unless proven otherwise.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9c12b45-5014-463d-9425-1f7abf72cd40",
                                                "sense_id": "b6e302ba-b629-3892-86dc-6241ae86aa52",
                                                "text": "Is there a place for heterosexual cisgenders in Africa's queer movement?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b5ae67ce-c4b1-4d02-ae9a-505988d9cf12",
                        "source_entry_id": "ee94ced9-cc24-3e90-a7d6-ce2c7b5858e7",
                        "source_sense_id": "2fd57234-4e3d-3bc8-828b-f5cb5ff0785c",
                        "target_lang_word": "cisgendered",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cisgendered",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71f7288b-e4e5-3232-a946-e6458d9e4fc4",
                                        "entry_id": "46fb29cc-6238-3074-a2fa-e388b2cdef21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of cisgender."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "uncommon"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de9025ff-fc4d-4da1-a12e-9a9193e65702",
                                                "sense_id": "71f7288b-e4e5-3232-a946-e6458d9e4fc4",
                                                "text": "They seemed to be rather tense at first, and it was very funny to see that after talking for a while they found out that a TS guy is actually just a person you can have a chat and a giggle with, just like they are! Amazing, isn't it? 9:-) Anyway, kind of feels nice, the fact that you might have created understanding and compassion for another T* which you don't even know, through 'educating' cisgendered people."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13aff424-dc73-410b-b9f8-6d7410116c2c",
                                                "sense_id": "71f7288b-e4e5-3232-a946-e6458d9e4fc4",
                                                "text": "Gendering is the process of classifying and identifying the gender of other people, quickly and usually unconsciously, based on just a few visual and/or audio clues. This process of gendering privileges cisgendered people as few cisgendered people have had the experience of being misgendered. The experience of being misgendered is common for all transgendered people before they transition and for many transgendered people after they transition."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "cisgendered",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "efde490c-069e-3fd7-b08c-c22b3256da0e",
                                        "entry_id": "f350d26a-c64b-30bf-abb9-e63a9258b95a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of cisgender."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "nonstandard",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e44f3fa5-d691-4430-aba6-19a93dd1658b",
                                                "sense_id": "efde490c-069e-3fd7-b08c-c22b3256da0e",
                                                "text": "The fact that many cisgendereds accept me as a woman despite the fact that my body is male and they know it says some cisgendereds accept the concept that 'person' defines gender. The fact that other cisgendereds and transgendereds(!) will only define my gender by my body shows that others reject the idea that gender is defined by person."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6b77261f-18e5-42c3-b063-dfc4f211b039",
                        "source_entry_id": "ee94ced9-cc24-3e90-a7d6-ce2c7b5858e7",
                        "source_sense_id": "2fd57234-4e3d-3bc8-828b-f5cb5ff0785c",
                        "target_lang_word": "cis",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cis",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bee56201-7ee5-3f5d-b33a-c2f18f4fb44f",
                                        "entry_id": "b1b693a5-6416-3e9d-be74-d6b6bc11817a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having two mutations on two genes on the same chromosome of a homologous pair."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ff3d492f-07c3-3bd1-aa87-59e1882dca5f",
                                        "entry_id": "b1b693a5-6416-3e9d-be74-d6b6bc11817a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of the side of the Golgi apparatus nearer to the endoplasmic reticulum."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5dae8b3c-3ba2-3fb6-8329-0dd386d954c3",
                                        "entry_id": "b1b693a5-6416-3e9d-be74-d6b6bc11817a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In (or constituting, forming, or describing) a double bond in which the greater radical on both ends is on the same side of the bond."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "physical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3dea11b-a1c5-49d1-84d1-148d416cf01d",
                                                "sense_id": "5dae8b3c-3ba2-3fb6-8329-0dd386d954c3",
                                                "text": "9 is thought to survive longer when the CH = CH bond is cis and to favour the formation of another cis double bond in a propagation reaction involving its displacement by monomer. 10, on the other hand, is more likely to yield a trans double bond […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1cf53032-9f7f-44b6-afa9-85c2a9d384e4",
                                                "sense_id": "5dae8b3c-3ba2-3fb6-8329-0dd386d954c3",
                                                "text": "However, a cis double bond causes a kink in the chain. (A cis double bond introduces a bend of about 42 into the linear hydrocarbon chain.)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06369e97-b567-4a80-a16c-e0147989c23f",
                                                "sense_id": "5dae8b3c-3ba2-3fb6-8329-0dd386d954c3",
                                                "text": "A cis double bond is one where the hydrogen atoms are both on the same side. In contrast, a trans double bond has them on the opposite side."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "09b3c075-09ee-31b3-951b-a078126e7950",
                                        "entry_id": "b1b693a5-6416-3e9d-be74-d6b6bc11817a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In (or constituting, forming, or describing) a coordination compound in which the two instances of a particular ligand are adjacent to each other."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "physical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "463e5296-8dba-43c1-87d0-72c1370add31",
                                                "sense_id": "09b3c075-09ee-31b3-951b-a078126e7950",
                                                "text": "The cis effect is the labilization of ligands which are cis to certain other ligands."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "cis",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ba389bba-83be-36ba-8bcb-3eeac4d8462a",
                                        "entry_id": "c0c97861-3df7-31c0-9315-91f70dcf5d88",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Cisgender (or sometimes cissexual): not trans (transgender or transsexual) nor non-binary."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9056f92-c1ff-4b74-840e-f731fa994ab3",
                                                "sense_id": "ba389bba-83be-36ba-8bcb-3eeac4d8462a",
                                                "text": "We're demonized and criminalized as perverts out to trick and deceive cis hetero men; therefore anything that happens to us, we 'had coming.'"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8489c0a-6074-495d-9985-0e7c9861551a",
                                                "sense_id": "ba389bba-83be-36ba-8bcb-3eeac4d8462a",
                                                "text": "Oh yeah, because you know who's been long overdue a challenge? The trans community. Oh, they've had their guard down for too long if you ask me. They'll all be checking their privilege on the way home now thanks to you, you brave little cis boy!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dfdbffb9-b2ec-492d-9c56-809696640243",
                                                "sense_id": "ba389bba-83be-36ba-8bcb-3eeac4d8462a",
                                                "text": "The reality is that LGBTQ+ people face challenges at disproportionally higher rates than their straight counterparts — drug use, sex work, and financial instability can be an unfortunate result. My privilege as a young cis white man whose parents weren't going to let me drown afforded me the ability to make those mistakes and live to talk about it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
